.claude/session-state.json

# graphify — knowledge graph IS tracked (team setup); only local-machine
# artefacts are excluded (cost log, pinned interpreter path, dated
# curated-graph backups the rebuild hook writes).
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/.graphify_python
# Tool-versioned AST cache: derived data, rebuilt offline by `graphify update`,
# and keyed by the graphify version. Tracking it made every upgrade a commit that
# deletes one version tree and adds another (0.9.9 -> 0.9.41 was 529 files, 40 MB)
# without telling a reader of this repository anything. What IS tracked, and what
# the tracking decision was actually about, is the structure map itself:
# graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md and wiki/.
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/

# Usage-gate artifact (scripts/claude_usage.py output)
claude-usage.txt

# The harness builds into its own workspace root, and the repo's `/target/` rule
# is anchored, so this directory needs its own line. Without it every harness
# build leaves the tree dirty, which breaks both the clean-status release check
# and the harness's own assertion that it leaves no trace in the repo.
smoke/target/

# The harness is a BINARY and wants a reproducible build, so its lock is tracked.
# The bare `Cargo.lock` pattern above matches at any depth and would swallow it.
!smoke/Cargo.lock
